<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yury of Zvenigorod</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1374–<a href="/years/1434">1434</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Yury Dmitrievich · Of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rurik-dynasty">Rurik dynasty</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Yury of Zvenigorod was a son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dmitry-donskoy">Dmitry Donskoy</a> and prince of Zvenigorod and Galich. When his brother Vasily I died in 1425, he claimed the throne of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a> against his nephew Vasily II under the old rule of succession from brother to brother, opening a long civil war. He twice seized Moscow, in 1433 and 1434, and died there as grand prince in 1434.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/yury-of-zvenigorod.jpg" alt="Yury of Zvenigorod" width="320" height="661" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Anonymous Russian painter (1670s-1917) Public domain image (according to PD-Russia-expired) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Frescos_in_Cathedral_of_the_Archangel_in_Moscow_-_west_wall_01_-_Yuri_of_Zvenigorod.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The principle was tested in the civil war of 1425–1453, when Vasily II fought his uncle <b>Yury of Zvenigorod</b> and his cousins Vasily Kosoy and Dmitry Shemyaka; Vasily was captured by the Tatars of Ulugh Muhammad in 1445 and blinded by his rivals in 1446, yet regained the…</blockquote><a href="/empire/grand-duchy-of-moscow">Grand Duchy of Moscow · Governance &amp; Law</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pereslavl-zalessky">Pereslavl-Zalessky</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/russia">Russia</a>. Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/russia">Russia</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=56.74,38.86&amp;year=1413" aria-label="Pereslavl-Zalessky on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5389 237 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Yury of Zvenigorod"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5839 507h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5839 507h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=56.74,38.86&amp;year=1413">What was here in 1413? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
